# Radharc (D107): the compositor, on the boot framebuffer (a physical VMO
# under its MMIO resource, as the console maps it), its latch thread on a
# deadline profile (the system resource). It takes the framebuffer from
# the console through the console's handoff, reads kbdfs's /dev/kbd and
# the mouse's /dev/mouse, and serves each client its own tree at
# /svc/windows. Only in the desktop's images: while it holds /dev/kbd,
# the console's shell hears no keys.
service windows
program radharc
resource mmio
resource system
bootdata
export per-client
use console
mount /dev kbdfs
mount /dev mouse after
mount /lib/theme bootfs/lib/theme
mount /lib/fonts bootfs/lib/fonts
restart on-failure
